{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they shall take to you oil</b> etc. The verse returns to it on account of 'upon the pure menorah' etc., because in this book, which is the Torah of the priests, it sets forth the order of all the utensils of the Tabernacle and the sacrifices and the ordination of the priests and the disqualifications of impurity that restrict entry to the Sanctuary and eating of holy things, and now it comes to explain the order of the menorah and the table, for the two are interdependent, and the incense has already been mentioned in the section of אחרי מות. And by right the section of the showbread should have preceded the section of the menorah, since the menorah was included in the showbread, as it is written ״ואת המנורה נוכח השלחן״ — except that he wanted to juxtapose the section of the blasphemer to the section of the showbread, as Rashi explained." "<b>To cause a lamp to ascend always.</b> Even on the Sabbath, even in impurity."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:50.064529286Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}